  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "The unit vector in ZOX plane, making angles $45^{\\circ}$ and $60^{\\circ}$ respectively with $\\vec{\\alpha}=2 \\hat{i}+2 \\hat{j}-\\hat{k}$ and $\\vec{\\beta}=j-\\hat{k}$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "T60kw",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\hat{i}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\hat{j}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Sq4Za",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\hat{\\mathrm{i}}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\hat{\\mathrm{k}}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "bkLMz",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\hat{i}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\hat{j}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Vko6k",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\hat{i}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\hat{k}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hint: \r\nLet the vector be $\\vec{r}=x \\hat{i}+z \\hat{k} \\Rightarrow|r|=1$\r\n$\\vec{r} \\cdot \\vec{a}=|r| |\\vec{\\alpha}| \\cos 45^{\\circ}$\r\n$\\therefore 2 x-z=\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}}$\r\n$\\vec{r} \\cdot \\vec{\\beta}=|\\vec{r}| |\\vec{\\beta}| \\cos 60^{\\circ}$\r\n$z=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$\r\n$\\therefore \\mathrm{x}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$\r\n$\\therefore \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{r}}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\hat{i}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\hat{k}$",
    "image": null
